From 4b91179205133fc69592ea87b3b1ba1d19e7297e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:58:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] debug(allwinner): PM event trace page and runtime
 experiment knob

Bring-up aid only, not for upstream. The Allwinner BL31 console has no
runtime scope and printing from PSCI handlers after the OS has gated the
UART clock would hang BL31, so record PM events in the last page of the
BL31 DRAM reservation instead (SUNXI_PM_TRACE_BASE = 0x4003f000, mapped
non-cacheable, a system ring plus one lock-free ring per core, survives
warm resets; the per-core rings freeze after a warm reset until the OS
re-arms them) where the OS (/dev/mem) or U-Boot (md.l) can read them.
The page carries a layout version, so a page left behind by a BL31 with
another layout is cleared rather than misread. Sleep events record
CPUIDLE_STAT and CPUIDLE_PEND | CPUIDLE_WAKE << 8; system suspend also
records the DRAM controller STATR/PWRCTL before suspend and what the
SRAM routine saw.

The same page carries a knob, reset to 0 at every boot, that selects
cpu-sleep experiments at runtime (0: WFI only with a warm restart,
1: the regular sequence, 3: the regular sequence with core 0 never
gated) and lets the system suspend path skip the DRAM self-refresh, the
CPU clock change or the SRAM relocation, or turn off the controller's
automatic power-down before requesting self-refresh. Mode 0 restarts the core
through the warm boot entry point instead of letting the generic code
panic on the returning WFI.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
